{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And it shall come to pass</b> — There is no doubt that this prophecy concerns the future, therefore he said: \"in the latter days.\" The reason: because he mentioned above that the mountain of the House shall become high places of a forest, he returned to comfort Israel that the glory of the House shall yet return. And it is known that the mountain of the House is not high, and behold the reason is that its fame shall go forth to afar, and from all directions they shall return to it with offerings, as though it were at the head of all the mountains, and it shall be raised above the hills, until all the inhabitants of the earth see it." "<b>And they shall stream</b> — They shall run, from the root נהר, for it is always running."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:00.587570197Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}